  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n@josepharhar @mfreed7 I just realized a pretty big part of the rendering story is still missing. I don't see any PR for the native/primitive appearance, as well as an allowance for user agents to render `img` elements in those modes as part of the `option` element's label (which I guess will have to be redefined to allow for some kind of structure). Is there test coverage for all the new markup features with `appearance: auto / none`?\n\n(Bit surprising this is overlooked given it is insisted upon for `<input type=checkbox switch>` to be able to land.)",
